sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor Client as Angular SPA / HTTP Client
    participant MW as Middleware Chain (Cors, RateLimit, Helmet, Auth)
    participant Route as Express Router & Zod Validation
    participant Controller as Module Controller (e.g. BookingController)
    participant Service as Domain Service (e.g. BookingService)
    participant Redis as Redis 7.0 In-Memory Engine
    participant Repo as Module Repository (Prisma Client)
    participant DB as MySQL 8.0 Database (ACID)
    participant Err as Centralized errorHandler

    Client->>MW: (1) HTTP POST /api/v1/booking/hold (Bearer Token, Payload)
    Note over MW: Verify CORS, Rate Limit, and decode JWT accessToken
    alt Invalid Token / Rate Exceeded
        MW-->>Client: Return HTTP 401 Unauthorized / 429 Too Many Requests
    end

    MW->>Route: (2) Pass sanitized request to matching route
    Note over Route: Parse request body against Zod Schema (booking.schema.js)
    alt Payload Validation Fails
        Route->>Err: Pass ZodValidationError
        Err-->>Client: Return HTTP 400 Bad Request (Field details)
    end

    Route->>Controller: (3) Forward validated DTO to controller handler
    Note over Controller: Extract params, user context, and invoke domain logic

    Controller->>Service: (4) Call service method: holdSeats(userId, showtimeId, seatIds)
    
    Service->>Redis: (5) Execute Atomic Lua Script (SET NX seat:lease:...)
    alt Any Seat Already Leased
        Redis-->>Service: Return Lock Conflict
        Service-->>Controller: Throw SeatUnavailableException
        Controller->>Err: Pass Conflict Error
        Err-->>Client: Return HTTP 409 Conflict (Seats currently held by another user)
    end

    Service->>Repo: (6) Begin Prisma Transaction ($transaction)
    Note over Repo,DB: Query ShowtimeSeat FOR UPDATE<br/>Verify version & create Booking (PENDING)<br/>Set activeLock = showtimeSeatId
    Repo->>DB: Execute SQL Queries inside ACID Transaction
    DB-->>Repo: Transaction Committed Successfully
    Repo-->>Service: Return Booking Entity with Countdown

    Service-->>Controller: (7) Return business domain result
    Controller-->>Client: (8) Return Standard JSON Envelope: HTTP 201 Created<br/>{ success: true, data: { bookingId, expiresAt: 900s, seats: [...] } }

